      "text": "[Skip to main content](https://www.un.org/www.un.org#main-content)\n\n# International Years\n\nYoung people attend the launch of the 2010 International Year of Youth on the theme \"\"Dialogue and Mutual Understanding\"\", inside the General Assembly Hall, at UN Headquarters. UN Photo/Paulo Filgueiras\n\nThese are the international years currently observed by the United Nations. The United Nations designates specific days, weeks, years and decades as occasions to mark particular events or topics in order to promote, through awareness and action, the objectives of the Organization. Usually, it is one or more Member States that propose these observances and the General Assembly establishes them with a resolution. On occasion, these celebrations are declared by the specialized agencies of the United Nations, such as UNESCO, UNICEF, FAO, etc., when they concern issues that fall within the scope of their competencies. Some of them may be later adopted by the General Assembly.\n\n## 2029\n\n[International Year of Asteroid Awareness and Planetary Defence](https://www.un.org/en/observances/asteroid-awareness-year)\n\n[A/RES/79/86](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/79/86)\n\n## 2027\n\nInternational Year of Sustainable and Resilient Tourism\n\n[A/RES/78/260](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/78/260)\n\n## 2026\n\nInternational Year of the Woman Farmer\n\n[A/RES/78/279](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/78/279)\n\n## 2026\n\nInternational Year of Volunteers for Sustainable Development\n\n[A/RES/78/127](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/78/127)\n\n## 2026\n\n[International Year of Rangelands and Pastoralists](https://iyrp.info/)\n\n[A/RES/76/253](http://undocs.org/en/A/RES/76/253)\n\n## 2025\n\n[International Year of Quantum Science and Technology](https://quantum2025.org/en/)\n\n[A/RES/78/287](http://undocs.org/en/A/RES/78/287)\n\n## 2025\n\n[International Year of Cooperatives](https://social.desa.un.org/issues/cooperatives/un-international-year-of-cooperatives)\n\n[A/RES/78/289](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/78/289)\n\n## 2025\n\n[International Year of Glaciers' Preservation](https://www.un-glaciers.org/en)\n\n[A/RES/77/158](https://www.undocs.org/en/A/RES/77/158)\n\n## 2025\n\n[International Year of Peace and Trust](https://feature.undp.org/for-people-for-peace/)\n\n[A/RES/78/266](https://www.undocs.org/A/RES/78/266)\n\n## 2024\n\n[International Year of Camelids](https://www.fao.org/camelids-2024/en)\n\n[A/RES/72/210](http://undocs.org/A/RES/72/210)\n\n## 2023\n\nInternational Year of Dialogue as a Guarantee of Peace\n\n[A/RES/77/32](https://www.undocs.org/en/A/RES/77/32)\n\n## 2023\n\n[International Year of Millets](https://www.fao.org/millets-2023/home/en)\n\n[A/RES/75/263](http://undocs.org/en/A/RES/75/263)\n\n## 2022\n\n[International Year of Sustainable Mountain Development](https://www.decadeonrestoration.org/2022-was-international-year-mountains-here-why-it-matters)\n\n[A/RES/76/129](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/76/129)\n\n## 2022\n\nInternational Year of Basic Sciences for Sustainable Development\n\n[A/RES/76/14](https://undocs.org/en/A/RES/76/14)\n\n## 2022\n\n[Interna",
